; What a correctness witness needs from the direct LLVM frontend that does not
; need LLVM: the map from its loop-head predicates to the C program, and the
; rewriting of a solution of those predicates into invariants of that
; program.  Kept apart from lib/LLVMFront, which is optional, so that the
; top-level program and its tests build without the LLVM bindings.

(library
 (name LLVMWitness)
 (public_name CoAR.LLVMWitness)
 (libraries core zarith CoAR.common CoAR.ast)
 (synopsis "Loop invariants of the C program from a solution of the direct LLVM translation"))
